Section: 4.2. i2b2 Obesity Challenge 2008
Text: Adding obesity as an anchor produces a clear Obesity topic, including several medications known to cause weight gain (e.g., acebutolol, klonopin). The anchored OSA topic, however, is quite poor and in fact re- sembles the rather generic topic to which obstructive sleep apnea is assigned by Unsupervised CorEx. It includes many spurious or non-speciﬁc terms like drug.

